# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Captured audit artifacts. NEVER commit these.
#
# This repo is PUBLIC. A mirror of a client site can contain live credentials,
# proprietary source (via sourcemaps), and client-confidential content.
# Committing it converts a needle-in-a-haystack exposure into an indexed,
# cloneable, permanent one. These entries exist before the first `git add`
# for exactly that reason -- git history is append-only, so an artifact
# committed once cannot be un-shipped by ignoring it later.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
mirror-raw/
rendered/
har/
sourcemaps/
*.har

# Raw (unredacted) scanner output. Redacted derivatives in findings/ are safe;
# these are not.
.audit-raw/
findings/*.raw
findings/retire.json

# Generated fixture credentials. Synthetic, but credential-shaped -- keeping
# them out of history avoids tripping secret-scanning push protection and
# avoids adding 8 fake keys to the world's grep corpus.
fixture/site/assets/config.gen.js

node_modules/
.DS_Store
imports/
